<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tirumala Deva Raya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1570–<a href="/years/1572">1572</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tirumala Deva Raya was the brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aliya-rama-raya">Aliya Rama Raya</a> and founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aravidu-dynasty">Aravidu dynasty</a>, the last ruling house of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>. After the defeat at Talikota in 1565 he withdrew with the treasury and the nominal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sadashiva-raya">Sadashiva Raya</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penukonda">Penukonda</a>, and around 1570 took the throne himself. He divided the remaining empire among his sons, one of whom later ruled as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venkatapati-raya">Venkatapati Raya</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tirumala-deva-raya.jpg" alt="Tirumala Deva Raya" width="320" height="468" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Raksas_Tagdi_04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
